<title>USA: Kaye Group Q4 pro forma net falls slightly.</title>
<headline>Kaye Group Q4 pro forma net falls slightly.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					    THREE MONTHS  TWELVE MONTHS</p>
<p>					    1996    1995    1996   1995</p>
<p>					   (Restated)(a)</p>
<p>PRO FORMA NET INCOME(b)</p>
<p>Income before charge</p>
<p>in lieu of income taxes</p>
<p>  and minority interest	   $2,799  $3,165  $5,211 $6,309</p>
<p> Charge in lieu of income taxes    760   1,115   1,484  1,995</p>
<p>Income before minority interest  </p>
<p>					   2,039   2,050   3,727  4,314</p>
<p> Minority interest		     359     361     656    759</p>
<p> PRO FORMA NET INCOME		1,680   1,689   3,071  3,555</p>
<p> PRO FORMA NET INCOME PER SHARE   0.24    0.24    0.44   0.51</p>
<p>HISTORICAL NET INCOME</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>  and minority interest	    2,799   3,165   5,211  6,309</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for income taxes</p>
<p>					     760  (1,650)  1,484     21</p>
<p>Income before minority interest</p>
<p>					   2,039   4,815   3,727  6,288</p>
<p> Minority interest		     359     847     656  1,107</p>
<p> HISTORICAL NET INCOME	     1,680   3,968   3,071  5,181</p>
<p> HISTORICAL NET INCOME PER SHARE  0.24    0.57    0.44   0.74</p>
<p>Weighted average of shares outstanding</p>
<p>					   7,020   7,020   7,020  7,020</p>
<p>(a) The pro forma charge in lieu of income taxes for the fourth quarter of 1995 has been restated to properly reallocate the charge among the 1995 quarters.  This restatement does not have an impact on the 1995 full year results.  The effect of the restatement is to increase net income per share from $0.22 to $0.24 for the three months ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>(b) Prior to the combination on October 2, 1995, the tax on income of certain of the Company's subsidiaries was paid by the shareholders or partners of those subsidiaries and not by the Company.  Effective with the combination, the Company's income is included in a consolidated federal income tax return. The pro forma results shown above include a benefit in lieu of income taxes for 1995 which provides for taxes as if the Company had been taxed as a corporation.</p>
